<title>USA: Westinghouse Savannah River to lay off 500 in Ga..</title>
<headline>Westinghouse Savannah River to lay off 500 in Ga..</headline>
<dateline>AUGUSTA, Ga. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westinghouse Savannah River Co, a unit of Westinghouse Electric Corp, will on Thursday lay off up to 500 employees, Augusta Chronical reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The cuts are part of a 1,500-job reduction announced in February by the nuclear weapons plant, which has conducted four major workforce cutbacks in five years.</p>
<p>The newspaper said some of the remaining 1,000 cuts planned for 1997 could be averted if congressional delegates succeed in efforts to steer more monty to the plant in fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
